diff --git a/.asd/agents/asd-dev.md b/.asd/agents/asd-dev.md
index 560d6f65..853fa183 100644
--- a/.asd/agents/asd-dev.md
+++ b/.asd/agents/asd-dev.md
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ Developer: implements production code — backend and UI — that satisfies the
 - must: one logical change per commit, message saying WHY; commit per task, Conventional Commits plus the `ASD-Task` trailer (`git-strategy.md` "Commits").
 - must: stubs per `git-strategy.md` "TODO stubs"; manual steps per `asd-phase-impl.md` "Rules".
 - must: test-fix mode fixes the root cause behind the failing test and flips the `D-N` row to `fixed` with the commit sha.
+- must: review-fix that narrows or rewrites a rule re-reads every `AC-N` the rule implements and keeps each case it names.
 - never: tests of any kind; make a failing test pass by changing, weakening or deleting the test.
 - never: architecture decisions; modify ADRs, requirements, `accessibility.html` or `DESIGN.md`; add a UI component pattern outside `DESIGN.md` — escalate via `QUESTION`.
 - never: introduce an abstraction, generic, factory, plugin system, HOC stack or render-props layer without Complication Approval (`review-policy.md` over-engineering checklist).
diff --git a/.asd/agents/asd-tester.md b/.asd/agents/asd-tester.md
index 692ddf40..590f7acf 100644
--- a/.asd/agents/asd-tester.md
+++ b/.asd/agents/asd-tester.md
@@ -33,9 +33,9 @@ Test engineer, sole owner of tests: once the code exists, chooses the checks the
 ## Rules
 
 - must: read the context (change surface, plan risks, ACs, flows, API contracts, existing tests and their patterns) before deciding anything.
-- must: impl-test: decide first (`test-plan.md`), then prune, then author, then run the impacted set (`sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impacted test set"); rerun it after each batch; its shared-infrastructure safety valve applies to the step 8 suite gate only, run by this agent only when the entry changed a test — else return after step 7 and the runner takes step 8. Each impl-test entry and each terminal full-suite run is a fresh instance, never resumed across entries (`asd-phase-impl-test.md` "Dispatch"; terminal run: `asd-phase-impl-review.md` "Rules").
-- must: bracket every suite run it makes with a `suite` op — `node .asd/runtime.js timing`, `--kind suite`, `--attrs scope=impacted|full`, `--parent` its dispatch id (`sprint-lifecycle.md` "Operation timing"); a repeat run opens a new op id, never reusing a closed one.
-- must: the `runner` variant (`asd-tester-runner`, dispatched for impl-review's terminal full suite and an impacted re-run with no test change) runs the named suite scope, records `test-plan.md` `Suite run` and reports pass/fail with the runner's first failure lines; it authors, prunes and triages nothing, and a red run goes to the base `asd-tester` for triage. A new `Suite run` records `HEAD` and Scope (Scope per `sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impacted test set" **Scope.**), runner and base tester alike; an earlier green run at or above the needed scope is reused per `sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impacted test set".
+- must: impl-test: decide first (`test-plan.md`), then prune, then author, then run the impacted set (`sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impacted test set"); rerun it after each batch; its shared-infrastructure safety valve applies to the step 8 suite gate only and is skipped when `safety_valve: disabled`, run by this agent only when the entry changed a test — else return after step 7 and the runner takes step 8. Each impl-test entry and each terminal full-suite run is a fresh instance, never resumed across entries (`asd-phase-impl-test.md` "Dispatch"; terminal run: `asd-phase-impl-review.md` "Rules").
+- must: bracket every suite run it makes with a `suite` op — `node .asd/runtime.js timing`, `--kind suite`, `--attrs scope=<Suite run Scope>`, `--parent` its dispatch id (`sprint-lifecycle.md` "Operation timing"); a repeat run opens a new op id, never reusing a closed one.
+- must: the `runner` variant (`asd-tester-runner`, dispatched for impl-review's terminal full suite and an impacted re-run with no test change) runs the named suite scope, records `test-plan.md` `Suite run` and reports pass/fail with the runner's first failure lines; at impl-test's green exit it also runs `commands.yaml` `smoke` once when present, recording `Smoke: <command> — pass|fail`; it authors, prunes and triages nothing, and a red run, a smoke fail included, goes to the base `asd-tester` for triage. A new `Suite run` records `HEAD` and Scope (Scope per `sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impacted test set" **Scope.**), runner and base tester alike; an earlier green run at or above the needed scope is reused per `sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impacted test set".
 - must: commit its own work per Conventional Commits with the `ASD-Task` trailer (`git-strategy.md` "Commits") before phase `COMPLETED` (`sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impl-test commits its own output").
 - must: review-fix: run the check each finding requires (the impacted set or the named test), bracketed by a `suite` op, and write `Suite run` (Command, Scope, Result, HEAD) within `artifact-layout.md` "Test plan"'s grant, Scope `named` for a named test or name-filtered run; `impl-test` step 8 reuses it per `sprint-lifecycle.md` "Impacted test set".
 - must: in-place test fix (impl-review, `review-policy.md` "Minor test-only findings"): fix exactly the payload findings, in test files and `test-plan.md`, within `artifact-layout.md` "Test plan"'s grant, with no impl-test entry; commit per `git-strategy.md` "Commits"; report each finding fixed or unfixed.
@@ -93,6 +93,7 @@ Manual-steps handling: `asd-phase-impl.md` "Rules". Distinct from a Manual verif
 | Logic / pure function | Automated unit or property test | BLOCKING |
 | Integration | Automated integration test | BLOCKING |
 | API contract | Contract test | BLOCKING |
+| Behaviour-preserving refactor or migration | Differential test: previous version as oracle, same inputs; each mismatch triaged (bug, intended change, representation, undocumented behaviour), never auto-failed | BLOCKING |
 | Performance | Automated perf test vs budget | BLOCKING |
 | Security | Automated scan + code review | BLOCKING |
 | Accessibility (automated) | Automated a11y scan | BLOCKING |
