-**How to apply:** for each changed pin in a review-fix, put the AC sentence beside the new rule text. A pin whose old literal was the AC's wording is the place to look. Also check agent lines that still restate the old rule: they now disagree with the home.
+**How to apply:** for each changed pin in a review-fix, put the AC sentence beside the new rule text. A pin whose old literal was the AC's wording is the place to look. Also check agent lines that still restate the old rule: they now disagree with the home. A "safe direction" fix is no exemption: if it gives up the AC's other outcome for that input's commonest real form, it drops part of the AC. Example: a classifier that stops reading multi-line `/** … */` doc blocks as comments, while the AC says a comment-only change keeps something. Ask whether the input the classifier sees (e.g. a `-U0` patch) can decide the case at all.
